<title>USA: Bigmar yr shr loss $0.51 vs $0.07 loss. [CORRECTED 08:10 GMT 19/4]</title>
<headline>Bigmar yr shr loss $0.51 vs $0.07 loss. [CORRECTED 08:10 GMT 19/4]</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Ohio 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects to add parentheses around figures in table to show loss where applicable.)</p>
<p>				 BIGMAR INC AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>		CONSOLIDATED CONDENSED STATEMENTS OF OPERATIONS</p>
<p>					   Year Ended December 31,</p>
<p>						 1996	     1995</p>
<p> Net Sales			$   7,931,149   $   5,600,362</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p>  Research and development	  801,560	    23,144</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>     administrative		 3,006,546	 1,493,055</p>
<p>Settlement fees paid</p>
<p>to a related party and</p>
<p>write-off of licensing</p>
<p>     fees				 511,777</p>
<p> Operating income (loss)	  (1,700,927)	(82,272)</p>
<p> Net income (loss)		  (1,639,544)	(97,204)</p>
<p> Net income (loss)  per share	  (0.51)	  (0.07)</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>  outstanding			 3,235,137	 1,337,292</p>
<p>Note: The company said it will be required to raise substantial funding for its expansion plans.</p>
<p>The company said it expects to be able to fund operations through July, and is discussing the availability of financing wih financial institutions.</p>
<p>The company said it incurred significantly higher research expenses in 1996 than in 1995 because it was preparing its manufacturing plant in Barbengo, Switzerland for commerical production, and was developing new oncology products.</p>
<p>The company said it expects sales and gross margins to improve once new products are added to the oncology line.</p>
